{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-027", "score": 0.127, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-027 | Study family SF-APPS-027: Adaptation quality vs talent as predictor of series wins\n- observed_research_question: Adaptation quality vs talent as predictor of series wins\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: pct_ran_BEST - pct_ran_AVOID predicts series wins after controlling for RS net-rating talent.\n- observed_result: corr(talent, adapt)=+0.124. Per-series logistic: talent_diff_z +0.737 p=0.0213; adapt_diff_z +0.328 p=0.2755. Team-in-series cluster: talent p=0.0095, adapt p=0.2449. Univariate adapt beta=+0.311 p=0.1128. LPM: talent +0 [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:confounding\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:CONFOUNDING\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: After talent control adapt p=0.275; n~55 series cannot separate coaching adaptation from roster quality.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=55 series / 110 directions"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-009", "score": 0.1, "document": "# FAM:SF-CHT-009 | Study family SF-CHT-009: Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type\n- observed_research_question: Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: Named star initiators have identifiable lineup and forced-play-type suppressors in the possession graph.\n- observed_result: Jokic vs MIN lineup PPP 0.814, -0.385 (n=59); Curry vs HOU 0.851, -0.358 (n=47); Doncic vs LAC 0.733, -0.396 (n=30); Giannis forced PULL_UP 0.848, -0.540 vs preferred DRIVE (largest gap).\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE\n- observed_failure_evidence: No placebo or matching; later sequence work treated similar star-chain gaps as artifacts.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n>=30 for lineup cells cited\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_method: Jokic/Curry/Doncic/Giannis; min-15 gate on 8 play types; opposing DEFENSE_LINEUP ~84% coverage; 272-row CSV."}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-037", "score": 0.086, "document": "# FAM:SF-CHT-037 | Study family SF-CHT-037: Sequence-memory lag effects with game-state controls\n- observed_research_question: Sequence-memory lag effects with game-state controls\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: Naive lag-1 play-type PPP effects survive period/clock/margin controls and within-team baselines.\n- observed_result: Lag-1 real, lag-2 small, lag-3+ ~0: d(1)=+0.024 AUC, d(2)=+0.004. SPOT_UP lag-1 MWU_p=0.0000 with and without controls. DRIVE lag-1 MWU_p=0.0000 but ctrl_p=0.0911. PNR naive p=0.031, controlled 0.136, within-team lift -0 [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- observed_failure_evidence: DRIVE and PNR lag-1 effects disappear with game-state controls / within-team baseline.\n- observed_sample_and_power: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPS-073\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-CHT-029\n- observed_verdict: null"}, {"id": "FAM:SF31", "score": 0.075, "document": "# FAM:SF31 | Study family SF31: Routing prior vs H2H posterior gate diagnostic\n- observed_research_question: Routing prior vs H2H posterior gate diagnostic\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: The n>=15 H2H gate suppresses real player-routing signal.\n- observed_result: [APPM-015] Mean PPP delta lead-default +1.259 (n>=5) to +1.129 (n>=15); low-n leaders are role players with 2-3 PPP on 5-7 possessions.\n- observed_result: [CHT-017] At n=5-9 typical leaders are 1-shot 3.00-PPP role players. Mean PPP delta lead-vs-default +1.26 at n>=5 and +1.13 at n>=15, inflated by small-sample distortion. n>=15 routing-override gate judged to filter nois [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: [APPM-015] Apparent +1.13 PPP edge is small-sample inflation (e.g. n=6, PPP=3.00).\n- auto_confidence: high (1.0)"}], "n_results": 4}

